@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s40b-youth`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 40B. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from line 1652 before the rules were run; none edited.
-- Tax year 2026: its first day is 1 January 2026, its last 31 December 2026. A person has completed n years on his nth birthday.
-- For one born on 15 June 2010: 15 on 1 January 2026, 16 from 15 June 2026, 16 on 31 December: last day yes, some day yes, every day no.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 40B`

GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `resident`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `born`      IS A DATE
      `spouse`    IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH AN `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B`
`in` `the year` `, resident:` `resident` `, the individual born` `born` `, the spouse born` `spouse` MEANS
    `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B` OF `the year`, `resident`, `born`, `spouse`, FALSE

GIVEN `born` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B`
`a resident individual with no spouse, born` `born` MEANS
    `An individual and a spouse, for section 40B` OF 2026, TRUE, `born`, NOTHING, FALSE

§§ `The individual alone, tax year 2026`

-- Born 15 June 2009: 16 on 1 January 2026 (turned 16 in June 2025), 17 on 31 December (turns 17 on 15 June 2026). All three readings: yes.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2009 6 15)) EQUALS 1
-- Born 15 June 2010: 15 at the start, 16 at the end. Last day yes (1), some day yes (1), every day no (0): the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 6 15)) BECAUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on the last day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 6 15)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on some day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 6 15)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on every day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 6 15)) EQUALS 0
-- Born 15 June 2008: 17 on 1 January 2026, 18 on 31 December. Last day no (18 is not under 18), some day yes (17 until 15 June), every day no.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 6 15)) BECAUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on the last day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 6 15)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on some day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 6 15)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on every day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 6 15)) EQUALS 0
-- Born 1 January 2010: his 16th birthday is the first day of the year: 16 on 1 January and on 31 December. Yes on all three.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 1 1)) EQUALS 1
-- Born 2 January 2010: 15 on 1 January, so not every day.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2010 1 2)) BECAUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"
-- Born 1 January 2008: 18 on 1 January 2026, so under 18 on no day: nothing on any reading.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 1 1)) EQUALS 0
-- Born 31 December 2008: 17 until the last day, when he turns 18: last day no, some day yes, every day no.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2008 12 31)) BECAUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"
-- Born 2011: 15 or 14 all year, and 2005: 20 or 21 all year: nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2011 6 15)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 2005 6 15)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`a resident individual with no spouse, born` (YMD 1990 6 15)) EQUALS 0

§§ `The spouse`

-- An adult whose spouse was born 15 June 2009: the spouse is 16-17 all year: one point.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 1990 6 15) `, the spouse born` (JUST (YMD 2009 6 15))) EQUALS 1
-- Both are 16 or 17: still one point.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 2009 3 3) `, the spouse born` (JUST (YMD 2009 6 15))) EQUALS 1
-- Neither: nothing. A spouse with a date of birth far from the age: nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 1990 6 15) `, the spouse born` (JUST (YMD 1991 6 15))) EQUALS 0
-- A spouse on the edge: born 15 June 2010 (some and last yes, every no): the default declines even though the individual is an adult.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 1990 6 15) `, the spouse born` (JUST (YMD 2010 6 15))) BECAUSE "section 40B does not say when in the tax year the age is measured, and here the readings differ"

§§ `Other tax years; fork F1; section 48A`

-- Tax year 2027: a person born 15 June 2010 is 16 on 1 January 2027 (turned 16 in June 2026) and 17 at the end: yes on all three.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2027 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 2010 6 15) `, the spouse born` NOTHING) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2023 `, resident:` TRUE `, the individual born` (YMD 2009 6 15) `, the spouse born` NOTHING) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, the individual born` (YMD 2009 6 15) `, the spouse born` NOTHING) BECAUSE "sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides"
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on the last day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, the individual born` (YMD 2009 6 15) `, the spouse born` NOTHING) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 40B, reading the age as` `on the last day of the tax year` `and the residence condition as` `an Israeli resident only` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `, the individual born` (YMD 2009 6 15) `, the spouse born` NOTHING) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 40B for` (`An individual and a spouse, for section 40B` OF 2026, TRUE, (YMD 2009 6 15), NOTHING, TRUE) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
